    "lawCode": "Amd §5, Chap 259 of 2004",
    "lawSection": "New York City",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7516\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 259 of the laws of 2004,\nrelating to enacting the Coordinated Construction Act for Lower\nManhattan, in relation to the effectiveness of the provisions of such\nchapter\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation would extend, until December 31, 2024, the\nCoordinated Construction Act for Lower Manhattan.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Coordinated Construction Act for Lower Manhattan enacted in 2004\nwas in response to the damage suffered by Lower Manhattan from the\n2001 attack on the World Trade Center and aimed to assist both the\nState and New York City in reconstruction efforts. By authorizing the\nextension of the Coordinated Construction Act, the much needed and\nvery important reconstruction process for lower Manhattan will be able\nto continue.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is new legislation.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
